      "date": "2026-05-16T19:43:03.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings: EPS misses analyst expectations",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹45.99 (up from ₹39.63 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹26.1b (up 9.4% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹5.64b (up 16% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 22% (up from 20% in FY 2025). The increase in margin was driven by higher revenue. Revenue was in line with analyst estimates. Earnings per share (EPS) missed analyst estimates by 2.9%. Revenue is forecast to grow 8.9% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, compared to a 12% growth forecast for the Pharmaceuticals industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 4% per year but the company’s share price has increased by 26% per year, which means it is tracking significantly ahead of earnings growth.",
